WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.297 --> 00:00:10.018
Some things never change.

2
00:00:10.698 --> 00:00:13.800
For example, mice have always been afraid of cats.

3
00:00:14.861 --> 00:00:17.542
When cats are hunting, some mice are lucky.

4
00:00:18.303 --> 00:00:19.243
Others are not.

5
00:00:20.844 --> 00:00:24.086
The mice in Cheese Town never knew when a cat might appear.

6
00:00:24.606 --> 00:00:26.868
They couldn't tell how many cats were near.

7
00:00:28.852 --> 00:00:31.053
There was no safe place for a mouse.

8
00:00:31.854 --> 00:00:33.295
Cats were everywhere.

9
00:00:35.096 --> 00:00:38.598
Finally, the mice realized that they had to do something.

10
00:00:39.198 --> 00:00:40.879
They decided to hold a meeting.

11
00:00:40.899 --> 00:00:45.521
"Quiet, please," said Mr.

12
00:00:45.581 --> 00:00:47.483
Whiskers, the mayor of the mice.

13
00:00:47.503 --> 00:00:51.505
"As you know, we have a big problem with cats.

14
00:00:52.445 --> 00:00:53.466
What can we do?"

15
00:00:53.786 --> 00:00:54.346
he asked.

16
00:00:55.087 --> 00:00:56.948
A mouse named Luke waved his hand.

17
00:00:58.008 --> 00:00:58.909
"Yes, Luke?

18
00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:00.729
Do you have any ideas?"

19
00:01:01.049 --> 00:01:01.650
asked Mr.

20
00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:05.691
Whiskers. "We can make cat traps!"

21
00:01:05.992 --> 00:01:07.152
Luke said excitedly.

22
00:01:07.172 --> 00:01:10.994
"Instead of cheese, we can use fake mice."

23
00:01:11.014 --> 00:01:14.815
"Any other ideas?"

24
00:01:15.255 --> 00:01:16.456
Mr. Whiskers asked.

25
00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:18.437
"Yes, Alice?"

26
00:01:20.338 --> 00:01:23.279
"We can poison them," suggested Alice.

27
00:01:24.259 --> 00:01:30.835
"When the cats are sleeping, we can put poison in their milk."

28
00:01:30.915 --> 00:01:32.196
Mr. Whiskers shook his head.

29
00:01:32.216 --> 00:01:34.438
"Any more ideas?"

30
00:01:35.459 --> 00:01:37.540
All the mice began to speak at once.

31
00:01:38.421 --> 00:01:40.162
Every mouse had a different idea.

32
00:01:41.083 --> 00:01:43.384
Then, a wise old mouse stood up.

33
00:01:45.726 --> 00:01:48.047
He spoke slowly and quietly.

34
00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:54.192
"If we could hear a cat coming, then we could hide."

35
00:01:55.092 --> 00:01:57.494
"But how will we hear if a cat is coming?"

36
00:01:58.054 --> 00:01:59.375
Mr. Whiskers asked.

37
00:02:03.018 --> 00:02:05.280
The old mouse paused and thought.

38
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:11.844
"We can tie bells around the cats' necks while they are sleeping," he said.

39
00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:17.148
"When we hear a bell, we will know a cat is coming."

40
00:02:18.049 --> 00:02:19.910
All the mice stood up and cheered.

41
00:02:20.731 --> 00:02:22.072
It was a great idea!

42
00:02:22.992 --> 00:02:25.775
It seemed like all their troubles were solved.

43
00:02:25.796 --> 00:02:31.202
"But who will tie the bells to the cats?"

44
00:02:31.802 --> 00:02:33.144
asked a small mouse.

45
00:02:34.045 --> 00:02:35.627
Everyone stopped cheering.

46
00:02:36.488 --> 00:02:43.376
Finally, the old mouse spoke, "Some things are easier said than done."
